What is ECR in AWS?
--------------------
ECR Elastic container registry is a managed Docker container image repository service.
ECR used to store docker images

It is used to store, manage, version and secure container images (like Docker images) in the cloud

Think of it like:
------------------
-Docker buildes the image
-ECR stores the image
-ECS/EKS pulls and runs the image

Real-time example: Suppose you have a Python app:
--------------------------------------------------

  "docker build -t myapp ."

This creates a Docker image locally

Now you push it to ECR using the following command

  "docker push"

Now aws services like EKS, ECS, Lambda can pull and run it.

Simple Analogy:
----------------
Docker = Kitchen
used to prepare food
  -Build image
  -Run container
  -Package app


ECR = Refrigerator
used to store food
  -Save image
  -Version images
  -Share images


ECS/EKS = Restaurant staff
Used to serve food
  -Pull image from ECR
  -Run application

Docker Workflow (without ECR)
------------------------------
code --> Docker build -->Local image -->Docker hub --> server pull ---> Run

Problem:
  -Public by defualt
  -External registry
  -Less AWS integration

AWS ECR Workflow:
-----------------
code --> Docker build --> Push to ECR --> ECS/EKS pull -->Deploy

Better because:
  -IAM authentication
  -Private respositories
  -Encryption
  -Vulnerability scanning
  -Easy intergration with AWS CI/CD


